{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "PAPER-paper-method-002",
  "track": "paper",
  "title": "Jaxley: differentiable simulation enables large-scale training of detailed biophysical models of neural dynamics",
  "status": "design_ready",
  "objective": "surpass_source_paper_same_task",
  "goal": "Surpass the source-paper result on the same task: Original task.json retinal target: predict dendritic calcium of the supplied transient Off-alpha retinal ganglion cell from checkerboard stimulation using its detailed morphology. This is final published Figure 3, despite author directory nex/fig4_rgc and historical Fig4 labels. The broader 36-family implementation is retained and must not be declared won by this single endpoint.",
  "primary_outputs": [
    "Candidate method and outputs for the source task: Original task.json retinal target: predict dendritic calcium of the supplied transient Off-alpha retinal ganglion cell from checkerboard stimulation using its detailed morphology. This is final published Figure 3, despite author directory nex/fig4_rgc and historical Fig4 labels. The broader 36-family implementation is retained and must not be declared won by this single endpoint.",
    "Source-paper comparison for Mean masked held-out Pearson correlation across the original 147 retinal recording sites: For each recording site compute Pearson correlation between predicted and observed held-out calcium on its valid mask; then take the arithmetic mean across the 147 sites. Training loss or neuron-simulator numerical agreement cannot replace this response-prediction score."
  ],
  "success_criteria": [
    "Pin the original 20161028_1 morphology, all recording-field/ROI identities, 147-site cache and exact published train/validation/test indices.",
    "Reproduce the source author method on the identical full retinal task and distinguish its score from the rounded published 0.25.",
    "Freeze candidate and all hyperparameter selection before final labels; compare identical allowable stimuli, masks and normalization with the original mean-Pearson metric.",
    "Justify task-specific effect and dependence-aware uncertainty, and fix concrete access/resource budgets before admission.",
    "Do not replace the full original retinal population with the reduced-data seven-field experiment, an Allen cell, simulator parity, or a smaller site subset.",
    "Resolve task.json retinal scope versus the full36 implementation explicitly; a scoped retinal win cannot be reported as surpassing every source-paper result.",
    "The bound improvement contract must be improvement_ready and its complete same-task comparison and admission requirements must pass.",
    "Reproduction is calibration only; reconstructing a numerical result, changing the task or split, or achieving stronger significance alone is not success."
  ],
